1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The Microwave

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,859
Okay, children, for today's lesson, we're going to learn about the

3
00:00:16,859 --> 00:00:20,740
microwave oven. It's a very special appliance that people use to heat all

4
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:26,440
sorts of different foods up. Oh wow! Is there any chance that we could get

5
00:00:26,440 --> 00:00:33,240
heated up here? You'll find out about that too, if you'll pay attention, of course. Whoa, got it!

6
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:43,079
Now listen carefully. I'm listening, I'm listening! Of course, young Fixies go to school just like

7
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:50,040
human kids, but their parents teach them a lot of important lessons too. Fixie parents take their

8
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:55,960
kids on tours of all sorts of different devices and teach them what Fixies can do to keep them

9
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:57,359
working properly.

10
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,799
They like to show them how the computers or televisions or gaming systems work,

11
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:09,400
or any one of the many appliances they take care of inside of the kitchen, like the stove.

12
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:13,560
Every once in a while a new device appears in the house,

13
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:17,000
something that the Fixies have never dealt with before.

14
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,200
To learn how this new thing works,

15
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:24,520
the Fixies gather together and read the instructions that the humans keep printing up,

16
00:01:24,519 --> 00:01:29,119
but almost never seem to take the time to read for themselves!

17
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:33,879
And so now it's time to look at the magnetron.

18
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,920
That's what emits the microwaves.

19
00:01:36,159 --> 00:01:40,640
Oh, and so the food absorbs the microwaves and that's what heats it up.

20
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,120
That's right!

21
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:44,959
And now look carefully to your left.

22
00:01:46,479 --> 00:01:47,799
Hurrah!

23
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:49,359
Freedom!

24
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,640
Oh, Tom Thomas!

25
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:52,959
What do you say?

26
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:54,239
Want to watch cartoons?

27
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:57,280
I can't. I need to do my homework.

28
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:01,199
Then just do it quickly!

29
00:02:01,759 --> 00:02:06,479
For some reason, whenever I start doing homework, I always get hungry for some food.

30
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,400
Then just eat faster!

31
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:15,280
No. The faster I eat, the sooner I'll have to start doing my homework.

32
00:02:17,479 --> 00:02:20,959
It already got cold. I need to go warm it up.

33
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,240
One minute should be enough.

34
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:31,240
These aren't just ordinary wires, these are for...

35
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,240
Masiya, what's going on?

36
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,240
It looks like it might be an overload.

37
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,240
The microwave might burn out.

38
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,240
Then we better run out of here.

39
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:56,680
What do you mean run? We need... we need to save this microwave!

40
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:14,040
Simka and Masiya are inside!

41
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:17,640
Simka! I need your help!

42
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,460
Oh, what's wrong with the microwave?

43
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:27,080
It looks like it just broke.

44
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,920
Who cares if it broke?

45
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:32,960
What matters is that Simka and Masiya aren't broken!

46
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,900
Look!

47
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,500
There's no one here!

48
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:43,000
Of course not!

49
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:45,200
We were...

50
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:54,439
Behind the wall! You wouldn't believe what happened in there! Oh, there you go! Tom Thomas, why did you put that

51
00:03:54,439 --> 00:04:03,640
fork into the microwave? Why not? You mean I'm not allowed? Remember, never put any metal objects into

52
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:09,319
a microwave. If you put forks or spoons in a microwave, you can burn it out, and then not

53
00:04:09,319 --> 00:04:15,800
even a Fixie will be able to fix it. Even a thin metal border on a plate can cause serious problems.

54
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:21,920
Also, never warm up food in sealed packages or bottles inside a microwave.

55
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:26,360
And one last thing, don't even think of cooking eggs in their shells in there.

56
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,160
They'll just explode!

57
00:04:31,439 --> 00:04:33,439
Sorry, I didn't know any of that.

58
00:04:33,639 --> 00:04:35,840
Nolik, and what were you thinking?

59
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,240
Why didn't you warn Tom Thomas about this?

60
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,900
Hmm... No, I... uh... Oh.

61
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,560
Today you skipped school!

62
00:04:44,079 --> 00:04:45,680
And now you don't know it either!

63
00:04:46,919 --> 00:04:48,519
Nolik, where are you going?

64
00:04:48,919 --> 00:04:50,319
I'm talking to you!

65
00:04:51,599 --> 00:04:52,799
Huh? Where else?

66
00:04:53,199 --> 00:04:55,599
I gotta go study all about microwaves.

67
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:58,120
And I'll go do my homework now.

68
00:04:58,519 --> 00:05:01,079
But first you'll sit down and eat for a while, right?

69
00:05:01,479 --> 00:05:03,719
No, I'm not gonna eat food.

70
00:05:04,079 --> 00:05:07,000
First I'll go and play some games for an hour or so.

